AB  - The fiber reinforced polymer bar has the inherent advantages of light weight, high strength and corrosion resistance, which is considered as a preferable alternative for the conventional bar in harsh environment. In this paper, to solve the problems of the conventional FRP bars and the redundancy of yield strength for hybrid fiber reinforced polymer bars, a design method for hybrid fiber reinforced polymer bars with both tensile ductility and different strength grades was developed. Meanwhile, the target strength grade table based on the various types of carbon fiber was also proposed in the Appendix, and the designers could directly choose the appropriate materials, design parameters and target strength grades of hybrid fiber reinforced polymer bars from Appendixes A and B according to the demands for strength grades in hybrid fiber composite bars reinforced structural concrete. In addition, to verify the validity of this design method, a batch of hybrid fiber reinforced polymer bars selected from target strength grade table were self-produced in the laboratory. A total of 40 specimens with different strength grades were prepared and tested to study their tensile properties. The results indicated that both the target strength grade and tensile ductility of hybrid fiber reinforced polymer bars were well achieved on the basis of this design method, and the predicted values were in agreement with the experimental results. © 2021 Elsevier Ltd
