AD  - RV College of Engineering, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Bengaluru, 560059, India
AD  - RV College of Engineering, Department of Information Science and Engineering, Bengaluru, 560059, India
AD  - RV College of Engineering, Department of Civil Engineering, Bengaluru, 560059, India
AB  - The standard accounting framework which depends only on production and consumption metrics cannot accurately depict all interrelated elements of present-day international supply chains. The restriction creates environmental accountability problems which impact various nations and industries while making it difficult to implement carbon border adjustment regulations. ClimateAuditX develops its complete network analysis system to study cross-border carbon flows through its detailed framework. A data processing system is created that produces standardized results through our 193-country trade study which uses international trade databases and sector-emission-intensity data to generate a complete international trade network showing all trade connections between 38,912 trade pairs. Our mirror reconstruction protocol improves data acquisition and network design through enhanced data gathering methods which boost network connections from 24,105 to 38,912 edges while solving all cases of isolated nodes. The structural enhancements provide essential support for all upcoming modeling procedures. The Heterogeneous Graph Neural Network (HGNN) module leverages this enhanced network to model multiple entity types and relation semantics across 15 economic sectors, achieving 0.8123 AUC-ROC (3× 5 -fold cross-validation) in carbon leakage risk classification across all 193 UN member states. ClimateAuditX further employs Shapley value allocation methods to distribute responsibility among supply chain participants based on their marginal contributions to global trade-embedded emissions.  © 2013 IEEE.
